{"Title":"An Act relative to parking violations in the town of Provincetown","BillNumber":"S2743","DocketNumber":"SD3187","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2024-04-19T11:47:23.113"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2024-04-19T11:47:23.1133333"},{"Id":"SKP1","Name":"Sarah K. Peake","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SKP1","ResponseDate":"2024-04-19T11:47:23.1266667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2743/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Cyr, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2743) of Julian Cyr and Sarah K. Peake (by the vote of the town) for legislation relative to parking violations in the town of Provincetown.  Transportation.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding sections 20A or 20A1/2 of chapter 90 or any general or special law to the contrary, the select board of the town of Provincetown may establish a schedule of fines for parking violations. The fines in said schedule shall not exceed $100; provided, however, that the fine for the violation of parking a motor vehicle within a posted shall be $100; and provided, further, that the fine for the violation of parking a motor vehicle within 10 feet of a fire hydrant shall not be more than $150; and provided, further, that the fine for the violation of parking a motor vehicle in violation of handicap parking rules or regulations shall not be more than $300. \r\n\tSECTION 2. The schedule of fines authorized pursuant to section 1 may provide that fines paid after 21 days of issuance but before the parking clerk reports to the registrar as provided in said sections 20A or 20A1/2 be increased by up to $25, and increased up to $50 if paid after such report to the registrar. \r\n\tSECTION 3. This act shall take effect upon its passage. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[{"Description":"S2743 -- Provincetown parking","DownloadUrl":"http://malegislature.gov/api/DownloadReport?attachmentId=18156&title=S2743%20--%20Provincetown%20parking"}],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable with Changes","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[{"AmendmentNumber":"1","ParentBillNumber":"S2743","Branch":"Senate","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2743/Branches/Senate/Amendments/1/"}]}